---
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';

const socials = [
  { href: SITE.links.youtube, label: 'YouTube' },
  { href: SITE.links.instagram, label: 'Instagram' },
  { href: SITE.links.whatsapp, label: 'WhatsApp' },
].filter((link) => link.href.length > 0);

/**
 * Licensing footnote. The reasoning lives in docs/adr/0010; only what constrains
 * this file is repeated here.
 *
 * This used to be the whole licensing statement inline, and it cost 305px on a 1280x900 desktop
 * (34% of the viewport) and 345px on a Pixel 7 (38%). Trimming words did not pay — cutting every
 * spare word saved ~11% of the characters, not even one line at 412px — and capping the width did
 * nothing on mobile, where the paragraph was already full width. The detail now lives on
 * /licenca/ and this is one line that points there.
 *
 * The licence NAMES are deliberately not here. "AGPL-3.0" and "CC BY-NC-SA 4.0" mean nothing to a
 * shop owner, and naming a licence without its conditions invites the reader to guess — guessing
 * wrong about NonCommercial and ShareAlike is exactly the defect review caught twice. Each name
 * also drags in a clause explaining it, which is what made this paragraph six lines long. The
 * names, all three CC conditions and the canonical texts are on /licenca/.
 *
 * The repository link STAYS. It is the AGPL-3.0 section 13 offer of Corresponding Source, and it
 * sits in the shared footer so a fork inherits the mechanism instead of having to remember it —
 * moving it to /licenca/ alone would mean a fork's users only meet the offer if they go looking.
 * A fork repoints SITE.repository.
 *
 * rel="noreferrer" only. noopener is inert without target="_blank", and nothing here opens a new
 * context. noreferrer is NOT redundant with the Referrer-Policy header: that header still sends the
 * origin cross-origin, whereas noreferrer sends nothing.
 *
 * data-pagefind-ignore is belt-and-braces — data-pagefind-body already scopes indexing to lesson
 * bodies, but this text repeats on every route, so it would pollute results if that ever moved.
 */
const linkClass = 'text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2';
---

<footer class="mt-16 border-t border-ink-100 bg-surface-alt">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-8 text-sm text-ink-700">
    <p class="font-semibold text-ink-900">{SITE.name}</p>
    <p class="mt-1 max-w-prose">{SITE.description}</p>

    {
      socials.length > 0 && (
        <ul class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
          {socials.map((link) => (
            <li>
              <a class={linkClass} href={link.href}>
                {link.label}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      )
    }

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-prose text-ink-500">
      Seu progresso fica salvo apenas neste aparelho. Não pedimos cadastro e não guardamos seus
      dados em nenhum servidor.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-500" data-licence data-pagefind-ignore>
      Código aberto no <a class={linkClass} href={SITE.repository} rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>. As
      aulas e as fichas podem ser compartilhadas e adaptadas — veja
      <a class={linkClass} href="/licenca/">licença e reúso</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</footer>
